{"duration_api_ms":95741,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9ac61699-755a-4324-b836-8faf4caa9bb5","total_cost_usd":0.16995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16574,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10365,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5527},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16574,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10365,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16574},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10365,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16574,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.16995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5527,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-parameter curve in flight_path_angle_deg. Every good design sits at D=3.3852, bluntness=1.2, cone=70. D is capped by heatshield_mass_fraction, which has near-zero margin (1.5e-5 to 1.8e-5) at D=3.3852. Bluntness and cone are capped by the aero-surface convex hull, since the 1.205 to 1.24 bluntness and cone=69 probes all failed extrapolation. Peak g is capped at 12 by gamma near -3.5703. Normalised hypervolume has plateaued at 0.3556 over the last five rounds. With one round and 24 evaluations left, the remaining gain is filling the gaps along the gamma line.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-9af34480dd37 and C-42bf20532268: gamma=-3.5703 gives g=12.0 with margin ~1.4e-5 to 2e-5, so this is the steep end of the front.\",\"C-895ab2d00f94: gamma=-1.5 is the shallow bound, with flux 227200 and T=417.87.\",\"Consecutive front points at gamma -1.5, -1.8, -1.9, -2.15, -2.3, -2.4 and -2.72 leave gaps of 0.1 to 0.32 deg. Flux and temperature vary smoothly and nearly linearly between them.\",\"C-2a109f1c4205 (D=3.36) has flux 277780 against 274560 at D=3.3852. Smaller D therefore costs flux and gives no compensating g benefit, so the D=3.3852 line stays dominant.\",\"C-7112b6b29bcf, C-14444dd6b10a, C-9961e7e6987c and C-67c6047be079: lowering bluntness or cone raises flux and violates the mass fraction, so they are dominated.\",\"Rows C-de59f8abeee6, C-ae614eb129f2, C-3d41ce848a30, C-98457c6f78bd and C-ea0e387c4c00 (geometry failures): stepping outside the hull wastes evaluations.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Flux falls with nose radius and lower ballistic coefficient, and bondline temperature falls with steeper entry because the soak is shorter. This is partly prior knowledge and partly fitted to the front rows. Since D, bluntness and cone are all at their limits, only gamma trades the two objectives. Filling gaps in gamma with linearly interpolated flux and temperature adds small but certain non-dominated points, and every proposal stays at the known-feasible D=3.3852.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The interpolated values assume smooth, near-linear variation. The true curve is slightly convex, so actual values may sit a little below the linear estimates, which would only help. Some gamma values may already have been evaluated in rows I cannot see. Gains per point are tiny because the front is nearly saturated. No exploratory off-line designs are included, since the data give no evidence that any beats this family.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228614,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.74,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a non-dominated point in the widest shallow gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.63},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229832,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.77,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.68},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230842,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.97,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.73},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231852,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.16,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap just before -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.77},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232663,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.51,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9af34480dd37\",\"rationale\":\"Midpoint between -1.8 and -1.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.85}